<%- include("partials/breadcrumbs", { items: [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "API" }
] }) %>

<section class="pt-6">
  <h1 class="text-balance font-bold tracking-tight">Model deprecation API</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-pretty text-base text-slate-700">
    Static JSON, served from the edge, CORS-enabled, no key and no rate limit.
    <%= modelCount %> models with status, dates, replacement and the sources behind them.
    MIT licensed — use it in a linter, a CI check, or a runtime guard.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-10">
  <h2 class="text-slate-900">Check one model</h2>
  <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"><code>curl <%= siteUrl %>/api/v1/models/<%= exampleId %>.json</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-700">
    The response carries both the authored <code class="font-mono text-xs">status</code> and a
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">computed_status</code> recalculated against the build date, so
    a model whose shutdown has passed reads <code class="font-mono text-xs">retired</code> without
    anyone editing data.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-10">
  <h2 class="text-slate-900">The whole catalog</h2>
  <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"><code>curl <%= siteUrl %>/api/v1/models.json</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-700">
    Ids are <code class="font-mono text-xs">provider/model</code>. Dated snapshots such as
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">gpt-4-32k-0613</code> are listed in an entry's
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">aliases</code> rather than duplicated as their own records.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-10">
  <h2 class="text-slate-900">Markdown, for agents</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-700">
    Every model page also exists as Markdown. Append <code class="font-mono text-xs">.md</code>.
  </p>
  <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"><code>curl <%= siteUrl %>/<%= exampleId %>.md</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="mt-10">
  <h2 class="text-slate-900">README badges</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-700">
    A shields.io endpoint per model. Green while it works, amber once deprecated, red once it is gone.
  </p>
  <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"><code>![](https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=<%= siteUrl %>/badge/<%= exampleId %>.json)</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="mt-10">
  <h2 class="text-slate-900">Feeds</h2>
  <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
    <li><a href="<%= icsPath %>" rel="nofollow" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover"><%= siteUrl %><%= icsPath %></a> — every shutdown as a subscribable calendar.</li>
    <li><a href="<%= rssPath %>" rel="nofollow" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover"><%= siteUrl %><%= rssPath %></a> — the changelog as RSS.</li>
    <li><a href="/llms.txt" rel="nofollow" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover"><%= siteUrl %>/llms.txt</a> — the agent-facing overview.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="mt-10">
  <h2 class="text-slate-900">JSON Schema</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-700">
    Every entry validates against a published schema. Put this line at the top of a YAML file for
    editor autocomplete:
  </p>
  <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"><code># yaml-language-server: $schema=<%= siteUrl %>/api/v1/schema.json</code></pre>
</section>
